{#
  Invitation to somebody who has NO account here yet.

  Flat HTML in the style of profile/claim_email.html.twig. The link in this one
  is more sensitive than any other email this app sends: until it is used, it is
  how this account's first password gets chosen. Hence the plain warning not to
  forward it.

  ── When Entra SSO arrives ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The middle paragraph becomes "sign in with your Microsoft work account" and
  the forwarding warning can soften — the link will no longer set a password.
  See DelegationManager::activateAccount().
#}
<p>Hello,</p>

<p>
  <strong>{{ inviterLabel }}</strong> has invited you to help keep the HMFP Search
  Tool profile for
  <strong>{{ physician.legalName }}{% if physician.credentials is not empty %}, {{ physician.credentials }}{% endif %}</strong>
  up to date.
</p>

<p>
  If you accept, you will be able to propose changes to this profile. A data
  steward reviews every change before it appears in the directory.
</p>

<p>
  You do not have an HMFP Search Tool account yet, so the link below will ask you
  to choose a password first. Your account will use this email address,
  {{ delegation.delegate.emailAddress }}. You can also decline, and no account
  will be set up.
</p>

<p><a href="{{ respondUrl }}">{{ respondUrl }}</a></p>

{% if expiresAt %}
  <p>
    This link stops working on
    {{ expiresAt|date('l j F Y') }} at {{ expiresAt|date('g:i A') }}.
  </p>
{% endif %}

<p>
  Please do not forward this email: the link sets up your account, and anyone
  holding it could set it up instead of you.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>If you were not expecting this, please do not use the link.</strong>
  Email <a href="mailto:{{ supportEmail }}">{{ supportEmail }}</a> or call
  (617) 278-8162 and let us know.
</p>
